6e93ec70cf045ddf4b743b1f51eaac2f.png)\n\nThe circle above is centered at $C(-4,-3)$ and the point $X(-1,0)$ lies on the circumference. Find the equation of the circle." :question/worked-solution "The general equation of a circle with radius $r$ centered at the point $(a,b)$ is\n\n$$\n(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2}={r}^{2}.\n$$\n\nThe length of the radius is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}CX & =\\sqrt{(-1-(-4))^{2}+(0-(-3))^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+{3}^{2}} \\\\  & =3\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, our circle is generated by the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2} & ={r}^{2} \\\\ (x-(-4))^{2}+(y-(-3))^{2} & ={(3\\sqrt{2})}^{2} \\\\ (x+4)^{2}+(y+3)^{2} & =18\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-117096/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3520d323-c6a4-5bce-bac1-1f4c02bd0068"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-117096"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-117099/selection/e31ccfa242e3800191d2e84fff4daddd279d43d61ab2d65243a25104f8ed6446" :answer/id #uuid "15b3f70f-e554-5518-a706-b6d9f8a3cafc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(x-4)^{2}+(y-3)^{2}=20" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117099/selection/c3e51838ed2dce88fc94b76a6f88ef50749dc44537468af040936a0737c29b7f" :answer/id #uuid "ae30da3a-2e62-55d6-a431-7ab0a1913fed" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(x-4)^{2}+(y-3)^{2}=2\\sqrt{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117099/selection/dcf2c206311f5ba837f0f10da2e912dcfed2448b185b62f9a7b1dbe7146c13a5" :answer/id #uuid "7af9df83-b0a8-5a34-8493-eb073834b16d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(x+4)^{2}+(y+3)^{2}=20" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117099/selection/c1fe7a01dd87ba9fa0ef0bddebccb1afb896035ef8f055a9c2e3fdb42211cb93" :answer/id #uuid "269fc353-dc05-5c54-89d2-62a3df2a2d93" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(x+4)^{2}+(y-3)^{2}=20" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {