n/math-academy-id "q-70990" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13957423/assets/a6a21dbf4785a270a0ae03066df1f92df73974532f9a75aa8e470cef42ea5e14.png)\n\nThe line segment $\\overset{―}{XY}$ is a diameter of a circle. Given that $X$ and $Y$ have coordinates $(-3,2)$ and $(3,4)$, respectively, what is the equation of the circle?" :question/worked-solution "The general equation of a circle with radius $r$ centered at the point $(a,b)$ is  \n\n$$\n(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2}={r}^{2}.\n$$\n\nUsing the distance formula to compute the distance between the points $X(-3,2)$ and $Y(3,4),$ we find that the length of the diameter is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}XY & =\\sqrt{{(-3-3)}^{2}+{(2-4)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-6)^{2}+(-2)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{40} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4\\cdot 10} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{10}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the radius of the circle is \n\n$$\nr=\\frac{2\\sqrt{10}}{2}=\\sqrt{10}.\n$$\n\nSince the center of a circle is the midpoint of the diameter, to find the center we use the midpoint formula as follows:\n\n$$\n(\\frac{{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}}{2},\\frac{{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}}{2})=(\\frac{-3+3}{2},\\frac{2+4}{2})=(0,3)\n$$\n\nSo our circle has radius $r=\\sqrt{10}$ and center $(a,b)=(0,3),$ and therefore it is represented by the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2} & ={r}^{2} \\\\ (x-0)^{2}+(y-3)^{2} & ={(\\sqrt{10})}^{2} \\\\ {x}^{2}+(y-3)^{2} & =10\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-70990/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "47863922-b0d5-5a0b-8a01-ffefe3b3c929"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-70990"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-117107/selection/9a3152c4f7ea205d90e86bbc1cf89c6745bb5be51ac0d1340634ded9c993e13c" :answer/id #uuid "b0f5f376-c804-5b50-8f8f-3001b438541d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(x-1)^{2}+(y-1)^{2}=8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117107/selection/2dde44301058dcd5c46df62d9ef9dc94c50b67bd59970c9c6b1d2f168af5e9f3" :answer/id #uuid "880b4123-f9d4-563f-a041-8b73dd2cace8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(x-1)^{2}+(y+1)^{2}=32" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117107/selection/32dbd7e89f2ebe57f6c6b81ff1d27f216704307eddde4ade256605deca50becb" :answer/id #uuid "e9db4eca-5680-5e3b-acba-9d164b085799" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(x+1)^{2}+(y-1)^{2}=8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117107/selection/68ae3a46866d42b51e0b5528b4ee7f43d27a1a4a493a7270fa48a3523dfe073f" :answer/id #uuid "a86e97af-bf35-5266-ac14-f8e11f7c34f6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(x-1)^{2}+(y+1)^{2}=8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117107/selection/95083d48ccbd321b6fe65d10c3625b939890daf054375397376e430e6b46d0ba" :answer/id #uuid "de3e8161-5edf-594f-890b-d802de0f0faa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(x+1)^{2}+(y-1)^{2}=32" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117107/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "2a66e7cc-9c0a-5d4e-9066-147a4750f027" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-117107/selection/68ae3a46866d42b51e0b5528b4ee7f43d27a1a4a493a7270fa48a3523dfe073f" :answer-field/choices ["q-117107/selection/9a3152c4f7ea205d90e86bbc1cf89c6745bb5be51ac0d1340634ded9c993e13c" "q-117107/selection/2dde44301058dcd5c46df62d9ef9dc94c50b67bd59970c9c6b1d2f168af5e9f3" "q-117107/selection/32dbd7e89f2ebe57f6c6b81ff1d27f216704307eddde4ade256605deca50becb" "q-117107/selection/68ae3a46866d42b51e0b5528b4ee7f43d27a1a4a493a7270fa48a3523dfe073f" "q-117107/selection/95083d48ccbd321b6fe65d10c3625b939890daf054375397376e430e6b46d0ba"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-117107" :question/id #uuid "99a09528-5597-5ef7-9025-8ce9688ffab6" :question/math-academy-id "q-117107" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13957423/assets/7f1573d17cb9a603727b644da6598355875b0be4b8c43a382e562155cb7a095c.png)\n\nThe line segment $\\overset{―}{XY}$ is a diameter of a circle. Given that $X$ and $Y$ have coordinates $(-1,-3)$ and $(3,1)$, respectively, what is the equation of the circle?" :question/worked-solution "The general equation of a circle with radius $r$ centered at the point $(a,b)$ is\n\n$$\n(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2}={r}^{2}.\n$$\n\nUsing the distance formula to compute the distance between the points $X(-1,-3)$ and $Y(3,1),$ we find that the length of the diameter is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}XY & =\\sqrt{(-1-3)^{2}+(-3-1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-4)^{2}+(-4)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16+16} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16\\cdot 2} \\\\  & =4\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the radius of the circle is \n\n$$\nr=\\frac{4\\sqrt{2}}{2}=2\\sqrt{2}.\n$$\n\nSince the center of a circle is the midpoint of the diameter, to find the center we use the midpoint formula as follows:\n\n$$\n(\\frac{{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}}{2},\\frac{{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}}{2})=(\\frac{-1+3}{2},\\frac{-3+1}{2})=(1,-1)\n$$\n\nSo our circle has radius $r=2\\sqrt{2}$ and center $(a,b)=(1,-1),$ and therefore it is represented by the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2} & ={r}^{2} \\\\ (x-1)^{2}+(y-(-1))^{2} & ={(2\\sqrt{2})}^{2} \\\\ (x-1)^{2}+(y+1)^{2} & =8\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-117107/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "47863922-b0d5-5a0b-8a01-ffefe3b3c929"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-117107"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-117106/selection/7b5998ca4804c3efa5d72408cfb3983ce5a608567846e7d7ecfd25e4df2bc243" :answer/id #uuid "609cc237-2c8e-5dbd-9c35-ebc41bc0426a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(x+1)^{2}+(y-1)^{2}=2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117106/selection/68ae3a46866d42b51e0b5528b4ee7f43d27a1a4a493a7270fa48a3523dfe073f" :answer/id #uuid "227c7605-dacb-5300-966b-ecef7af8fc05" :answer/type :a